🔄 Complete Saga Example

Now let's see where Saga actually happens.

Scenario 1 — Success

Send:

POST http://localhost:8081/orders
{
    "productName": "Laptop",
    "amount": 50000
}

Flow:

             Customer
                │
                ▼
       Order Service :8081
                │
                ▼
          Create Order
                │
                ▼
            CREATED
                │
                │ REST
                ▼
      Payment Service :8082
                │
                ▼
          Process Payment
                │
                ▼
             SUCCESS
                │
                ▼
       Order Service :8081
                │
                ▼
              PAID
❌ Scenario 2 — Payment Failure

Send:

POST http://localhost:8081/orders
{
    "productName": "Mobile",
    "amount": 0
}

Flow:

Order Service
      │
      ▼
Order CREATED
      │
      ▼
Payment Service
      │
      ▼
Payment FAILED ❌
      │
      ▼
Compensation
      │
      ▼
Order CANCELLED

Response:

{
    "id": 2,
    "productName": "Mobile",
    "amount": 0.0,
    "status": "CANCELLED"
}
🔁 Scenario 3 — Refund

If payment was successful:

Payment
   │
   ▼
SUCCESS
   │
   ▼
Something goes wrong
   │
   ▼
REFUND

Call:

PUT http://localhost:8082/payments/1/refund

Result:

SUCCESS → REFUNDED
📋 All APIs Together
| # | Service | Method | URL                     | Purpose             |
| - | ------- | ------ | ----------------------- | ------------------- |
| 1 | Order   | POST   | `/orders`               | Create order + Saga |
| 2 | Order   | GET    | `/orders`               | Get all orders      |
| 3 | Order   | GET    | `/orders/{id}`          | Get order           |
| 4 | Order   | PUT    | `/orders/{id}/status`   | Update order        |
| 5 | Payment | POST   | `/payments`             | Process payment     |
| 6 | Payment | POST   | `/payments`             | Test failed payment |
| 7 | Payment | GET    | `/payments`             | Get all payments    |
| 8 | Payment | GET    | `/payments/{id}`        | Get payment         |
| 9 | Payment | PUT    | `/payments/{id}/refund` | Refund payment      |


So you have 9 APIs across 2 microservices.

⭐ Most important API

For demonstrating Saga to your teacher/interviewer, use:

POST http://localhost:8081/orders

because this single API demonstrates:

Order Service
     ↓
Payment Service
     ↓
SUCCESS / FAILED
     ↓
PAID / CANCELLED

That's the core of your MicroService_Project-14-Saga project.
